@startuml
title TestNG example: worker fixtures and class state
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
hide footbox

participant "TestNG classes\nin one worker JVM" as tests
participant "TestInfrastructure\nlazy worker holder" as fixture
database "Worker-local\nPostgreSQL" as postgres
queue "Worker-local\nRabbitMQ" as rabbit

note over tests,rabbit
  ShardPilot selects whole class families before TestNG execution.
  TestNG parallel=none; data-provider rows also use parallel=false.
end note

tests -> fixture : Class A: inherited @BeforeClass
group First access only: Startables.deepStart(...).join()
  par PostgreSQL startup
    fixture -> postgres : Start with random mapped endpoint
    postgres --> fixture : Ready
  else RabbitMQ startup
    fixture -> rabbit : Start with random mapped endpoints
    rabbit --> fixture : Ready
  end
end
fixture -> postgres : CREATE DATABASE example_<generated A>
fixture --> tests : Store URL in Class A instance

loop Class A test methods / data-provider rows
  tests -> postgres : Fresh JDBC connection; isolated rows/tables
  tests -> rabbit : AMQP when required: private client / queue
  tests -> tests : Assert; close method-owned clients
end

tests -> fixture : Class B: inherited @BeforeClass
fixture -> postgres : CREATE DATABASE example_<generated B>
fixture --> tests : Class B URL; reuse the same service pair

note over tests,rabbit
  No @AfterClass container stop or cross-class test dependencies.
  Provider invocations stay with their test class's owner shard.
end note

tests -> tests : Worker exits after all selected classes
note over postgres,rabbit
  Ryuk removes the disposable containers on worker exit.
  Another shard / worker owns an independent fixture pair.
end note
@enduml
